  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U24", "U34", "U11"],
      "pins": ["U24.2", "U34.2", "U11.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "NET0014", "NET0054", "NET0176", "NET0138", "NET0005"],
      "obs": "On the 'LED Enable and E-Stop Config' sheet the three SN74LVC1G07 open-drain buffers U24, U34 and U11 have their data input (pin 2) tied directly to GND, while their /OE (pin 1) is the controlled line (pulled to +3V3 via R57/R24/R38 and switched low by SW9) and their outputs drive the LED_RED indicators D23/D22/D31 and the sink node NET0005.",
      "expected": "The specification states these buffers are 'wired as /OE-controlled sinks'. For a non-inverting open-drain buffer to act as a sink the input must be held HIGH (to +3V3 / the branch signal); with the input at GND the output is always high-impedance and can never sink.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "LED Enable and E-Stop Config sheet: U24 pin2 -> GND, U34 pin2 -> GND, U11 pin2 -> GND; /OE pins 1 -> NET0014/NET0054/NET0176 via 2.2k pull-ups; outputs -> LED_RED D23/D22/D31 and NET0005"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "gated through single non-inverting buffers (SN74LVC1G07, parts U15, U22, U35, U36) wired as `/OE`-controlled sinks, feeding an ESTOP_OUT signal"}
      ],
      "impact": "Because the buffer inputs are stuck low, the open-drain outputs never pull down. The per-branch e-stop indicator LEDs can never light, and the local motherboard e-stop branch (NET0005) can never assert the sink, so a local e-stop condition would not be signalled as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build otherwise matches the spec (16 MHz CAN crystals, LTC4412+PMOS ideal-diode, non-inverting SN74LVC1G07 buffers, 120R CAN termination, documented known issues), but the e-stop sink/indicator buffers U24/U34/U11 have their data inputs tied to GND instead of high, so they cannot function as the '/OE-controlled sinks' the specification describes."
}

